<title>UK: Card spending up 10 percent over Xmas - Barclays.</title>
<headline>Card spending up 10 percent over Xmas - Barclays.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Barclays Plc said on Sunday that cashpoint withdrawals and debit and credit card spending in the run-up to Christmas was up 10 percent.</p>
<p>In the week before Christmas, there was a 10 percent jump in the demand for cash as 372.3 million stg was dispensed through Barclays cash machines. The busiest day was December 21 when 71.4 million stg was dispensed.</p>
<p>Barclays said credit card company Barclaycard saw its nine million cardholders spend up to 1,500 stg per second over the festive season -- a 10 percent increase on last year.</p>
<p>-- Mike Peacock, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
